  <section class="intro" id="lines">
    <h2>Work projects</h2>
    <p>Three projects, newest first. signalSEO is my own product. At NFE I test and improve a live training platform on contract. At Microkeeper I spent two years on payroll software used by businesses across Australia.</p>
    <p>Each one shows what the software does, what I built and what it runs on. The recordings play when you reach them. Hover one to pause it, or pick a tab to skip ahead.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="route" style="--line:var(--purple)" aria-labelledby="r-signal">
    <div class="zone">
      <div class="badge"><b>signalSEO</b><span>2026 – now&ensp;·&ensp;Founder</span></div>
      <div class="notes">
          <h3 id="r-signal">My own product</h3>
          <p class="lede">SEO and business-positioning software that shows local businesses where they stand, what they're doing wrong and how to fix it, then keeps watch, so they rank better without the guesswork and get back to running their business.</p>
          <ol class="stops">
            <li><strong>Understand</strong><span>A plain-English report on where they rank, who's beating them, and why.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Monitor</strong><span>Rankings checked every night, plus rival moves and what Google's AI answer says.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Control</strong><span>A short list of fixes for the week, drafted by Claude and checked before anyone sees it.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Built on my own</strong><span>LLM integration, data pipelines from Firecrawl, DataForSEO and Google, and Stripe billing, with over 100 automated test files.</span></li>
          </ol>
          <ul class="status" aria-label="Stack"><li>TypeScript</li><li>Node</li><li>Express</li><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>Claude API</li><li>Firecrawl</li><li>DataForSEO</li><li>Stripe</li></ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="viewer tabs" data-viewer style="--line:var(--purple);--ar:16/10" aria-label="signalSEO">
        <div class="screen">
          <div class="slide on"><div class="shot"><video data-chapters src="/assets/videos/signal-ride.mp4" poster="/assets/videos/signal-ride-poster.webp" muted playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="signalSEO site: the rival check, then each section in turn"></video></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="track">
          <button class="play" type="button" aria-label="Pause"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path class="i-pause" d="M6 4h3v12H6zM11 4h3v12h-3z"/><path class="i-play" d="M6 4l10 6-10 6z"/></svg></button>
          <ol class="stations" aria-label="Chapters">
            <li><button type="button" data-t="0" data-note="Paste a website and see who outranks it, built from scraped pages and live Google data.">Rival check</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="4.03" data-note="Owners get one clear answer instead of hundreds of keywords.">One answer</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="11.14" data-note="Claude drafts the wording for each fix, and automated checks run before it's shown.">Report &amp; fixes</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="17.4" data-note="Every night it reads Google's AI answer and flags whether it cites you or a rival.">AI answers</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="23.98" data-note="Every number says where it came from: measured, estimated or written by AI.">Sources</button></li>
          </ol>
          <span class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fill"></span></span>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="caption" aria-live="polite"></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="route flip" style="--line:var(--rose)" aria-labelledby="r-nfe">
    <div class="zone">
      <div class="badge"><b>NFE</b><span>Oct 2026 – now&ensp;·&ensp;Contract</span></div>
      <div class="notes">
          <h3 id="r-nfe">Testing and improving a live platform</h3>
          <p class="lede">A training platform that takes beauty therapists from application to certificate. I test it, fix what I find, and ship approved changes for participants, tutors and admins using Claude Code.</p>
          <ol class="stops">
            <li><strong>60 acceptance tests</strong><span>Then automated the click-through checks with AI agents and Playwright.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Public site rework</strong><span>The homepage, training, register and sign-in pages, to an approved design.</span></li>
            <li><strong>One design system</strong><span>Labels, icons and tables that look the same for every role.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Support desk</strong><span>Staff can fix sign-in problems, and every action is logged.</span></li>
          </ol>
          <ul class="status" aria-label="Stack"><li>TypeScript</li><li>Claude Code</li><li>Playwright</li><li>Clerk</li><li>Replit</li></ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="viewer tabs" data-viewer style="--line:var(--rose);--ar:16/10" aria-label="NFE training platform">
        <div class="screen">
          <div class="slide on"><div class="shot"><video data-chapters src="/assets/videos/nfe-ride.mp4" poster="/assets/videos/nfe-ride-poster.webp" muted playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="NFE public site: opening sequence, then each section in turn"></video></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="track">
          <button class="play" type="button" aria-label="Pause"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path class="i-pause" d="M6 4h3v12H6zM11 4h3v12h-3z"/><path class="i-play" d="M6 4l10 6-10 6z"/></svg></button>
          <ol class="stations" aria-label="Chapters">
            <li><button type="button" data-t="0" data-note="The homepage I reworked, from its opening animation down.">Opening</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="5.1" data-note="Three ways to train, laid out side by side.">Course formats</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="12.35" data-note="How the training works, step by step.">Learning flow</button></li>
            <li><button type="button" data-t="19.03" data-note="Where the course leads: a recognised certificate.">Certification</button></li>
          </ol>
          <span class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fill"></span></span>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="caption" aria-live="polite"></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="route" style="--line:var(--blue)" aria-labelledby="r-mk">
    <div class="zone">
      <div class="badge"><b>Microkeeper</b><span>2024 – 2026&ensp;·&ensp;Full stack</span></div>
      <div class="notes">
          <h3 id="r-mk">Payroll, connected and faster</h3>
          <p class="lede">Two years on a payroll and workforce platform, taking small modules from requirements through to release and checking them in production.</p>
          <ol class="stops">
            <li><strong>Xero and Reckon</strong><span>Connected both accounting suites, so pay runs reach the books without anyone re-typing them.</span></li>
            <li><strong>50 seconds to 3</strong><span>Indexes and reworked queries sped up key pages for businesses with up to 10,000 staff.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Process automation</strong><span>A profile image pipeline on Cloudflare Images for thousands of users, and onboarding letters from templates.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Skills HR and Super Funds</strong><span>Reworked layout and workflow, including on phones.</span></li>
          </ol>
          <ul class="status" aria-label="Stack"><li>PHP</li><li>MySQL</li><li>JavaScript</li><li>REST APIs</li><li>OAuth</li><li>Chart.js</li><li>Cloudflare Images</li></ul>
